=== p2-windows · W7 · page:automations/ActionBuilder (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:automations/ActionBuilder   kind=page   web route=(unrouted)
Web source  : web/src/features/automations/pages/ActionBuilder.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); feature surfaces live under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection +
  diagnostics + registration, unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged state
  holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's idealized "ActionBuilder.xaml +
  ActionBuilderViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Automations" is mapped onto these real conventions.
- This unit PRE-EXISTED on disk as a near-complete implementation (apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/
  ActionBuilder.cs + ActionBuilder.Model.cs + ActionBuilder.ViewModel.cs, namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews)
  with a comprehensive headless test (TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/ActionBuilderTests.cs, already
  Compile-linked in TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj). It built and tested clean, but it was never ledgered and had
  a parity DEFECT: 5 placeholder strings used non-web *Hint key names (commandParamsHint / notifyHint /
  settingKeyHint / valueNumberHint / valueTextHint) — keys ABSENT from the .resw catalog — which dodged the
  ADR-011 placeholder scanner (the literal "Placeholder" is a forbidden stub marker) at the cost of diverging
  from the manifest/web key names. That divergence was invisible to the value-based unit tests.
- FIX (surgical): renamed the 5 key constants' VALUES to the web/manifest *Placeholder keys
  (commandParamsPlaceholder / notifyPlaceholder / settingKeyPlaceholder / valueNumberPlaceholder /
  valueTextPlaceholder), each annotated `// parity:allow web i18n key name, not a stub marker` — the
  documented opt-out (mirroring the repo's existing TsInput/TsSelect/TsTextarea PlaceholderText uses) so the
  placeholder gate stays clean while the keys now match the web verbatim. The web English fallbacks were
  already correct, so the existing value-based tests still pass unchanged.
- i18n catalog: the manifest's commandParamsObjectError row was MISSING from Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw
  and is now added; the surface's two extra native a11y/empty keys (automations.builder.empty,
  automations.builder.region) were also added so EVERY visible literal is catalog-sourced. The other 24
  required keys + the 5 corrected *Placeholder keys already existed in the catalog. Keys are resolved with the
  web's natural names (no "translation." prefix) through the ILocalizer → Localization bridge, identical to the
  completed admin/ApiLogs unit.
- Web route is "(unrouted)" — ActionBuilder is a controlled sub-component consumed by the automation builder
  page, not a navigable destination — so NO NavigationView registration is added (consistent with the sibling
  unrouted feature-views AutomationActivityFeed / AutomationCard, which are likewise not shell-registered).
- Added one regression test (Surface_resolves_every_manifest_string_key) that pins all 27 manifest keys by
  name through a RecordingLocalizer — guarding against any future revert to the non-web *Hint keys.
- SI units: N/A (the surface carries no measurements; no SI conversion applies).

